@startuml
title Customer UI Flow
start
:Login;
:Account Dashboard /customer;
note right
  Tile grid: one tile per owned account
  (primary first, then created_at ASC).
  Tile: displayName, owner accountNumber, balance, Primary badge.
  Transaction rows/detail: maskedNumber only.
  Tap tile → /customer/transactions?accountId=<id>
end note
:Select account tile;
:Transactions list /customer/transactions?accountId=<id>;
note right
  Account selector (shared presentational component).
  URL is the only selection state.
  No accountId → resolve primary/first, history.replace.
  Direction: All / Money In / Money Out (accessible radio group).
  Search merchant/reference; filter status/date/amount; sort; 1-based page.
end note
:Search merchant/reference; filter direction/status/date/amount;
:Choose sort and 1-based page;
:Open transaction details /customer/transactions/:id;
note right
  Back link returns to list preserving accountId + filters.
  Back from list → account dashboard.
  Completed transactions without an existing dispute show a
  keyboard-accessible row chevron. Expanding the row smoothly reveals
  Raise dispute without changing the merchant link to transaction details.
end note
:Raise dispute /customer/disputes/new?transactionId=<uuid>;
note right
  Reload transaction details; show merchant, amount, reference,
  and masked account only. Desktop shows summary beside the form;
  mobile stacks summary above it. Choose reason, describe, submit directly.
  Confirmation says case received/open; it does not promise a refund.
  Customer dispute history/detail routes remain deferred.
end note
stop
@enduml
